# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "`if` statement {#if-statement}"
msgstr "`if` statement {#if-statement}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `if` statement is used to conditionally perform operations based on the value of a classical bit or register.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ang `if` statement para magsagawa ng mga operasyon nang kondisyonal batay sa halaga ng isang classical bit o register.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the example below, we apply a Hadamard gate to a qubit and measure it. If the result is 1, then we apply an X gate on the qubit, which has the effect of flipping it back to the 0 state. We then measure the qubit again. The resulting measurement outcome should be 0 with 100% probability.\n"
msgstr "Sa halimbawa sa ibaba, nag-aaplay kami ng Hadamard gate sa isang qubit at sinusukat ito. Kung ang resulta ay 1, nag-aaplay kami ng X gate sa qubit, na may epektong ibabalik ito sa estado na 0. Pagkatapos ay sinusukat namin ang qubit muli. Ang nagreresultang kinalabasan ng pagsukat ay dapat na 0 na may 100% na posibilidad.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow/extracted-outputs/f0f191a7-d59d-415f-a11b-9f39e431269b-0.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow/extracted-outputs/f0f191a7-d59d-415f-a11b-9f39e431269b-0.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `with` statement can be given an assignment target which is itself a context manager that can be stored and subsequently used to create an else block, which is executed whenever the contents of the `if` block are *not* executed.\n"
msgstr "Ang `with` statement ay maaaring bigyan ng assignment target na isa ring context manager na maaaring i-store at pagkatapos ay gamitin para lumikha ng else block, na isinasagawa tuwing ang mga nilalaman ng `if` block ay *hindi* isinasagawa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the example below, we initialize registers with two qubits and two classical bits. We apply a Hadamard gate to the first qubit and measure it. If the result is 1, then we apply a Hadamard gate on the second qubit; otherwise, we apply an X gate on the second qubit. Finally, we measure the second qubit as well.\n"
msgstr "Sa halimbawa sa ibaba, nagpapasimula kami ng mga register na may dalawang qubit at dalawang classical bit. Nag-aaplay kami ng Hadamard gate sa unang qubit at sinusukat ito. Kung ang resulta ay 1, nag-aaplay kami ng Hadamard gate sa pangalawang qubit; kung hindi, nag-aaplay kami ng X gate sa pangalawang qubit. Sa wakas, sinusukat namin ang pangalawang qubit din.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow/extracted-outputs/d40249f1-d951-49e4-9ee9-662d3568f32f-0.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow/extracted-outputs/d40249f1-d951-49e4-9ee9-662d3568f32f-0.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to conditioning on a single classical bit, it's also possible to condition on the value of a classical register composed of multiple bits.\n"
msgstr "Bukod sa pag-condition sa isang classical bit, posible rin ang pag-condition sa halaga ng isang classical register na binubuo ng maraming bit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the example below, we apply Hadamard gates to two qubits and measure them. If the result is `01`, that is, the first qubit is 1 and the second qubit is 0, then we apply an X gate to a third qubit. Finally, we measure the third qubit. Note that for clarity, we chose to specify the state of the third classical bit, which is 0, in the `if` condition. In the circuit drawing, the condition is indicated by the circles on the classical bits being conditioned on. A solid circle indicates conditioning on 1, while an outlined circle indicates conditioning on 0.\n"
msgstr "Sa halimbawa sa ibaba, nag-aaplay kami ng Hadamard gate sa dalawang qubit at sinusukat ang mga ito. Kung ang resulta ay `01`, iyon ay, ang unang qubit ay 1 at ang pangalawang qubit ay 0, nag-aaplay kami ng X gate sa ikatlong qubit. Sa wakas, sinusukat namin ang ikatlong qubit. Tandaan na para sa kalinawan, pinili naming tukuyin ang estado ng ikatlong classical bit, na 0, sa kondisyon ng `if`. Sa drawing ng circuit, ang kondisyon ay ipinahiwatig ng mga bilog sa mga classical bit na kina-condition. Ang isang solidong bilog ay nagpapahiwatig ng pag-condition sa 1, habang ang isang bilog na may balangkas ay nagpapahiwatig ng pag-condition sa 0.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow/extracted-outputs/6ccfd81b-0bda-409e-bd9a-116848df631b-0.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow/extracted-outputs/6ccfd81b-0bda-409e-bd9a-116848df631b-0.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Switch statement {#switch-statement}"
msgstr "Switch statement {#switch-statement}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The switch statement is used to select actions based on the value of a classical bit or register. It is similar to an if statement, but you can specify more cases for the branching logic. The example below applies a Hadamard gate to a qubit and measures it. If the result is 0, apply an X gate on the qubit, and if the result is 1, apply a Z gate. The resulting measurement outcome should be 1 with 100% probability.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ang switch statement para pumili ng mga aksyon batay sa halaga ng isang classical bit o register. Katulad ito ng isang if statement, ngunit maaari kang tumukoy ng mas maraming kaso para sa branching logic. Ang halimbawa sa ibaba ay nag-aaplay ng Hadamard gate sa isang qubit at sinusukat ito. Kung ang resulta ay 0, mag-aaplay ng X gate sa qubit, at kung ang resulta ay 1, mag-aaplay ng Z gate. Ang nagreresultang kinalabasan ng pagsukat ay dapat na 1 na may 100% na posibilidad.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow/extracted-outputs/04b82e33-7c95-4042-a5e9-d00ff075ca02-0.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow/extracted-outputs/04b82e33-7c95-4042-a5e9-d00ff075ca02-0.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the example above used a single classical bit, there were only two possible cases, so you could have achieved the same result using an if-else statement. The switch case is mainly useful when branching on the value of a classical register composed of multiple bits. The following example shows how to construct a default case, which is executed if none of the preceding cases are. Note that in a switch statement, only one of the blocks are ever executed. There is no fallthrough.\n"
msgstr "Dahil gumamit ang halimbawa sa itaas ng isang classical bit lamang, dalawa lang ang posibleng kaso, kaya maaari mong makamit ang parehong resulta gamit ang isang if-else statement. Ang switch case ay pangunahing kapaki-pakinabang kapag nagba-branch sa halaga ng isang classical register na binubuo ng maraming bit. Ang sumusunod na halimbawa ay nagpapakita kung paano bumuo ng default case, na isinasagawa kung wala sa mga naunang kaso ang tumugma. Tandaan na sa isang switch statement, isa lamang sa mga block ang isinasagawa. Walang fallthrough.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example below applies Hadamard gates to two qubits and measures them. If the result is either 00 or 11, apply a Z gate to the third qubit. If the result is 01, apply a Y gate. If none of the preceding cases matched, apply an X gate. Finally, measure the third qubit.\n"
msgstr "Ang halimbawa sa ibaba ay nag-aaplay ng Hadamard gate sa dalawang qubit at sinusukat ang mga ito. Kung ang resulta ay alinman sa 00 o 11, mag-aaplay ng Z gate sa ikatlong qubit. Kung ang resulta ay 01, mag-aaplay ng Y gate. Kung wala sa mga naunang kaso ang tumugma, mag-aaplay ng X gate. Sa wakas, sukatin ang ikatlong qubit.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow/extracted-outputs/6aaba57e-7841-47d3-8f31-f922cb2b81f7-0.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow/extracted-outputs/6aaba57e-7841-47d3-8f31-f922cb2b81f7-0.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "For loop {#for-loop}"
msgstr "For loop {#for-loop}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A for loop is used to iterate over a sequence of classical values and perform some operations during each iteration.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ang for loop para mag-iterate sa isang sequence ng mga classical value at magsagawa ng ilang operasyon sa bawat iteration.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following example uses a for loop to apply 5 X gates to a qubit and then measures it. Because it performs an odd number of X gates, the overall effect is to flip the qubit from the 0 state to the 1 state.\n"
msgstr "Ang sumusunod na halimbawa ay gumagamit ng for loop para mag-apply ng 5 X gate sa isang qubit at pagkatapos ay sukatin ito. Dahil nagsasagawa ito ng gansal (odd) na bilang ng mga X gate, ang pangkalahatang epekto ay baligtarin ang qubit mula sa estado 0 patungo sa estado 1.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow/extracted-outputs/c6c91715-7a98-46a8-885e-92d3d1f99557-0.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow/extracted-outputs/c6c91715-7a98-46a8-885e-92d3d1f99557-0.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "While loop {#while-loop}"
msgstr "While loop {#while-loop}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A while loop is used to repeat instructions while some condition is satisfied.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ang while loop para ulitin ang mga instruksyon habang natutugunan ang ilang kondisyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example below applies Hadamard gates to two qubits and measures them. Then it creates a while loop that repeats this procedure while the measurement outcome is 11. As a result, the final measurement should never be 11, with the remaining possibilities appearing with approximately equal frequency.\n"
msgstr "Ang halimbawa sa ibaba ay nag-aaplay ng Hadamard gate sa dalawang qubit at sinusukat ang mga ito. Pagkatapos ay lumilikha ito ng while loop na umuulit ng pamamaraang ito habang ang kinalabasan ng pagsukat ay 11. Bilang resulta, ang panghuling pagsukat ay hindi dapat maging 11, at ang natitirang mga posibilidad ay lalabas na may humigit-kumulang pantay na dalas.\n"

